# Riverpod

- Providers live in `features/<feature>/application/`. Name them
  `<thing>Provider`. Depend on other providers with `ref.watch`.
- Inject SDKs and config through providers (`firebaseAuthProvider`,
  `appConfigProvider`, `targetPlatformProvider`) so tests can override them.
  Do not call `FirebaseAuth.instance` from widgets.
- Widgets: `ConsumerWidget` or `ConsumerStatefulWidget`. `ref.watch` for
  state that rebuilds the UI; `ref.read` inside callbacks and `runAuthAction`.
- Repository methods throw only the feature's failure type (`AuthFailure`),
  never raw SDK exceptions. Map those in `data`.
- Auth UI runs async work through `AuthActionMixin.runAuthAction`. It
  ignores repeat taps, shows `AuthFailure.message`, and stays silent on
  cancellation.
- Routing: keep redirect decisions in the pure `authRedirect` function.
  `routerProvider` only bridges `authStateChangesProvider` into GoRouter.
  Use `authStateChangesProvider` for routing and `currentUserProvider` for
  display.

```dart
// BAD: widget reaches into Firebase
await FirebaseAuth.instance.signInWithEmailAndPassword(...);

// GOOD: widget calls the repository provider
await ref.read(authRepositoryProvider).signInWithEmail(
  email: email,
  password: password,
);
```
